        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Buildings: SNCI Tower, 8 Spruce Street\n- Places: TriBeCa, Manhattan, Lower Manhattan, New York City\n- People: Frank Gehry\n- Topics: building height, floor count, location, naming\n\nFacts:\n- SNCI Tower is planned to rise 289.6 metres (950 ft) in New York City's TriBeCa district.\n- SNCI Tower is planned to have 57 floors.\n- 8 Spruce Street was originally known as Beekman Tower and is currently marketed as New York by Gehry.\n- 8 Spruce Street is a 76-story skyscraper in Manhattan, New York City.\n- Frank Gehry designed 8 Spruce Street.\n- 8 Spruce Street is located at 8 Spruce Street between William Street and Nassau Street in Lower Manhattan, just south of City Hall Park and the Brooklyn Bridge.",
